### Configuration Variables
@base_url = https://localhost:7171/api/Transactions

### 1. Get All Regions
# Description: Fetch supported countries and their time zones.
# Expected Response: 200 OK with an array of Region objects.
# Example: [{ "id": 1, "name": "Israel", "timeZoneId": "Israel Standard Time" }, ...]
GET {{base_url}}/regions
Accept: application/json

###

### 2. Get Approved Transactions History
# Description: Fetch history with pagination.
# Expected Response: 200 OK with an array of TransactionResponseDto.
# Example: [{ "transactionId": "guid", "status": "Approved", "submittedTimeUtc": "..." }]
GET {{base_url}}/GetApprovedTransactions?page=1&pageSize=10
Accept: application/json

###

### 3. Create New Transaction (Should be Approved)
# Description: Testing a transaction during standard business hours (12:00 PM).
# Expected Response: 
# {
#   "transactionId": "matching-guid",
#   "status": "Approved",
#   "submittedTimeUtc": "2026-05-14T12:00:00Z"
# }
POST {{base_url}}/CreateTransaction
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "transactionId": "{{$guid}}",
    "regionId": 1,
    "submittedTimeUtc": "2026-05-14T12:00:00Z"
}

###

### 4. Create New Transaction (Should be Rejected)
# Description: Testing a transaction late at night (23:30 PM).
# Expected Response: 
# {
#   "transactionId": "matching-guid",
#   "status": "Rejected",
#   "submittedTimeUtc": "2026-05-14T23:30:00Z"
# }
POST {{base_url}}/CreateTransaction
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "transactionId": "{{$guid}}",
    "regionId": 1,
    "submittedTimeUtc": "2026-05-14T23:30:00Z"
}

###

### 5. Invalid Data Test (Error Handling)
# Description: Sending an empty body to test API validation.
# Expected Response: 400 Bad Request with validation error details.
POST {{base_url}}/CreateTransaction
Content-Type: application/json

{
}